<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19310" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gargĭlĭus</span></b> , a,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>name of a
			Roman</i> gens. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			Gargilius, <i>a famous hunter</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 6,
			58</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			Gargilius Martialis, <i>a Roman author of the third
				century of our era.</i>— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Deriv.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gargĭlĭānus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a Gargilius</i>, <i>Gargilian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fundus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 32, 1, 41, § 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
